  "id": "Hounslow-P_2026_0838",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Installation of a double sided internally illuminated digital display on the proposed communications hub",
  "development_type": "Other advertisements",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its siting and design, would result in an unnecessary and harmful addition to street clutter within this section of the public footway, where similar structures already exist in close proximity. The cumulative impact of these features would detract from the established character of the High Street and diminish the quality of the public realm. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policy D8 (Public Realm), Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC4 (Heritage) and CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures), and the aims of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed illuminated advertisement display sign with high illuminance level would introduce an incongruous addition which would harm the pedestrian experience along the street, and fail to preserve or enhance the character of the Turnham Green Conservation Area. It will adversely impact the setting of the heritage asset and open space. Therefore, the proposal is contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 CC4 and CC5.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its excessive scale, siting and design would result in an unacceptable level of obstruction to cyclist and pedestrian visibility and would adversely affect highway and pedestrian safety. The development would therefore be contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 (Developing a Sustainable Local Transport Network) and Policy CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures)."
  ],
